Package: zumir
Title: Native Code from R Without a Compiler, with 'MIR'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Vladimir", "Makarov", role = "cph",
           comment = "Author of the vendored 'MIR' library")
  )
Description: Brings 'MIR', a lightweight just-in-time compiler, to R. Other
    packages link to it through a versioned C interface to build functions
    and get native code back, or 'MIR' interpreter code where no code
    generator exists for the processor. R users can compile a short numeric
    C function, or a numeric R function in a documented subset of the
    language, to native code from R, with no system compiler installed.
